@@ -99,3 +99,28 @@ needed if a plugin's restore method itself raises.
 
 Python's bare ``isinstance`` does not invoke this protocol. Libraries should
 preserve any individual-check guarantees they need outside beartype.
+
+Invocation scopes
+-----------------
+
+``beartype.plug.get_hint_check_scope()`` returns a ``HintCheckScope`` for the
+nearest generated public check, or ``None`` outside checking. Scope creation
+is lazy: checks that never request state allocate no scope object. Parameters
+and returns share the decorated invocation. Nested decorated calls and public
+DOOR calls start separate scopes, while an internally delegated forward alias
+shares the enclosing scope. Checker caches preserve that distinction regardless
+of which path is used first.
+
+Use ``scope.state`` as a library namespace keyed by a private object, rather
+than a string another plugin might use. ``scope.arguments`` lazily provides
+bound function arguments, including defaults; standalone DOOR scopes provide
+an empty mapping. ``scope.owner_code`` identifies the generated entry point
+for explicit decorator integration; it is not an invocation identifier.
+Scope object identity distinguishes invocations. Scope lookup follows the
+live call stack, so copied execution contexts cannot resurrect completed scopes.
+
+Do not retain a scope past the check: its state and arguments may retain user
+objects. Scope objects themselves hold no frames or context tokens. Scope
+ownership does not replace state rollback: a rejected composite alternative
+must restore registered domains, and a rejected nested leaf must roll back even
+when a predicate catches the rejection and then succeeds.
